$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Procedure for DNA-Mediated
Enantioselective Fluorination of 1 A buffer solution of the DNA-bound
catalyst (1.3 mg/mL st-DNA and 0.3 mM of [Cu(dmbipy)(NO3)2]) prepared by
shaking a solution of DNA (20 mg of st-DNA, was dissolved in 7 mL of H2O
and 3 mL of 0.1 M MES,19 pH 5.5 mixture, prepared 24 h in advance) with
an aqueous solution of the catalyst {5 mL of a 0.9 mM solution, prepared
by adding 1.8 mg (0.0047 mmol) of [Cu(dmbipy)(NO3)2] in a minimal amount
of DMSO to 5 mL of H2O}. An aliquot of a stock solution of 1 in MeCN (30
mL of a 0.5 M soln, final concn 1 mM) was added and the mixture was
cooled to 5 °C. The reaction was started by addition of Selectfluor®
(10.8 mg, 0.030 mmol, final concn 2 mM) and shaken continuously for 6 h.
The reaction mixture was then extracted with Et2O, washed with brine,
dried over Na2SO4 and the solvent was evaporated under reduced pressure
to give crude 2. The product 2 was identified by the 1H NMR, 19F NMR
spectroscopy and HPLC directly on the crude reaction mixture on
comparison of the authentic sample prepared by previously reported
DBFOX-Ph/Ni(II) method.7a The yield was determined by 19F NMR analysis
with CF3Ph as an internal reference. The ee of 2 was determined by chiral
HPLC analysis (Chiralpak AD-H or Chiralcel OD-H column). Compound 2d,
yield 96%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, DNA used as chiral ligand, buffered soln., 70% ee
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM DNA-mediated enantioselective carbon-fluorine bond formation
