$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Preparation of α-Fluoroaldehydes and
α-Fluoroketones. To a stirred mixture of carbonyl compound 1 (1.0 mmol)
and (S)-proline 3a (0.3 mmol) in MeCN (2 mL) was added Selectfluor (1.5
mmol) in one portion at 0 °C. Afterwards trifluoro acetic acid (0.3 mmol)
was added and the reaction mixture was stirred at r.t. (0 °C in case of
the aldehydes) until the reaction was complete (monitored by GC).
Purification by flash chromatography or filtration through a short silica
plug, respectively, afforded the pure product 2. 2a: Yield 73%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Direct organocatalytic α-fluorination of aldehydes and ketones
