$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Preparation of
α-Fluoroaldehydes and α-Fluoroketones. To a stirred mixture of carbonyl
compound 1 (1.0 mmol) and (S)-proline 3a (0.3 mmol) in MeCN (2 mL) was
added Selectfluor (1.5 mmol) in one portion at 0 °C. Afterwards trifluoro
acetic acid (0.3 mmol) was added and the reaction mixture was stirred at
r.t. (0 °C in case of the aldehydes) until the reaction was complete
(monitored by GC). Purification by flash chromatography or filtration
through a short silica plug, respectively, afforded the pure product 2.
2-Fluorocyclohexan-1-one (2e): Yield 73%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ =
1.70 (m, 2 H, CH2), 1.88 (m, 1 H, CH2), 2.02 (m, 2 H, CH2), 2.34 (m, 1 H,
CH2), 2.56 (m, 1 H, CH2), 4.90 (dddd, J = 48.90, 11.26, 6.32, 1.22 Hz, 1
H, CHF) ppm. 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 22.75 (d, JC,F = 9.9 Hz, CH2),
26.91 (CH2), 34.18 (d, JC,F = 18.9 Hz, CH2), 40.21 (CH2), 92.58 (d, JC,F
= 188.9 Hz, CHF), 205.71 (d, JC,F = 188.9 Hz, C=O) ppm. 19F NMR (376 MHz,
CDCl3): δ = -188.23 (d, J = 50,5 Hz, CHF) ppm.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, optimization study, optimized on catalyst
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Direct organocatalytic α-fluorination of aldehydes and ketones
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Enders, Dieter; Huettl, Matthias R. M.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synlett (2005), (6), 991-993

